minih264e (animation.datatype's MP4 writer: its H.264 encoder), CC0 1.0
  file:   libraries/opendatatypes/classes/datatypes/animation/h264/minih264e.h
  from:   https://github.com/lieff/minih264, minih264e.h at commit
          b0baea7a80ef9d12da97301dd1099b8791b5ba43 (10 December 2020)
  sha256: 661afe7802b4e1174e8389632f3ee437b903e036a9c91a7f035830947c6a7aae (as fetched)
  ours:   upstream/minih264/minih264e-b0baea7-gfopendatatypes.patch, applied in
          the tree: big-endian fixes (intra 4x4 words, motion vector packing,
          the deblocking strength), AmigaOS's byte order, MINIH264_NO_SIMD
          (the plain C on a host, for the tests) and MINIH264_PADDED_INPUT
  licence: upstream/minih264/LICENSE (CC0 1.0, checked in the source's own
          header: "dedicated all copyright ... to the public domain")
  not used: minimp4 (same author, CC0): the MP4 muxer is our own
          (animation/mp4_core.c), for PCM sound and no writable data

